WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:17,140
I have a UTI and tried to treat it with the rife and the vannos but it wasn't working so I am now

00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:25,140
on nitro afiradol. Should I take a probiotic while I'm taking an antibiotic?

00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:35,680
Bottom rule, the bottom line rule, just across the board, if you have to take an antibiotic, you should take a probiotic with it.

00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:56,680
You can take it with it and mid between doses also. So let's say if you're taking the antibiotic twice a day, once in the morning, let's say you're taking a night of clock and once in the evening, let's say you're taking a six o'clock, you can take a probiotic at night of clock, take a probiotic at one o'clock and take another probiotic with your dose of antibiotic at six o'clock.

00:00:56,680 --> 00:01:10,680
There's been numerous studies that have come out that said if you take a probiotic and it wasn't even specific to what type of probiotic. So just take whatever you have, just take a probiotic, take a probiotic when you're taking the antibiotic.

00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:25,680
It was a sharp decrease in gut damage and loss of microbiota if you take a probiotic with an antibiotic. So the answer is yes.

